+# Windows ARM64 Port
+
+Native Windows ARM64 (`aarch64`) support for zstd 1.5.7, the source the MSYS2 recipe builds. It is on branch `arm64-port`.
+
+zstd's C library was already mostly ARM64-ready:
+- `lib/common/compiler.h` picks the NEON paths when `_M_ARM64` is defined.
+- The CMake build always defines `ZSTD_DISABLE_ASM` under MSVC, so the x86-64 `huf_decompress_amd64.S` is never compiled for ARM64.
+
+The port fills in three gaps:
+- The Visual Studio solution had no ARM64 platform.
+- Some code paths were guarded only by GCC's `__aarch64__` macro, so MSVC ARM64 lost them. These include prefetch, which compiled to a no-op under MSVC ARM64.
+- There was no Windows ARM64 CI job.
+
+## Summary of Changes
+### Build System
+- `build/VS2010/zstd.sln`: adds the `Debug|ARM64` and `Release|ARM64` solution configurations and their mappings for every project.
+- `build/VS2010/{libzstd,libzstd-dll,zstd,datagen,fullbench,fuzzer}/*.vcxproj`: adds ARM64 `ProjectConfiguration`, property groups and `ItemDefinitionGroup`s, copied from x64 with these exceptions:
+  - no `MachineX86`;
+  - no `OmitFramePointers` (`/Oy`, which is x86-only);
+  - no `EnableEnhancedInstructionSet` (x86 `/arch:`).
+- `build/VS_scripts/build.generic.cmd`: the help text now lists `ARM64` as a platform. The script passes the value through unchanged.
+- `build/cmake`: unchanged. It already works for MSVC ARM64.
+- `build/meson` and `Makefile`: unchanged.
+
+### Source Code
+These guards add MSVC ARM64 paths only. They are additive, and x64, x86, GCC/Clang aarch64 and ARM64EC behave as before.
+- Prefetch: in `lib/common/compiler.h`, an MSVC `_M_ARM64` branch maps `PREFETCH_L1`/`PREFETCH_L2` to the `__prefetch()` intrinsic. Before this they were no-ops on MSVC ARM64. `dumpbin /disasm` of `zstd.dll` shows 719 `prfm` instructions.
+- Prefetch call sites: `lib/compress/zstd_double_fast.c` (2 sites) and `lib/decompress/zstd_decompress_block.c` (`ZSTD_execSequence`) are widened from `__aarch64__` to `__aarch64__ || _M_ARM64`.
+- Endianness: in `lib/common/mem.h`, `MEM_isLittleEndian()` now returns a compile-time constant on MSVC `_M_ARM64`.
+- 64-bit detection: `programs/platform.h` now includes `_M_ARM64` in the `__64BIT__` check. This makes no functional difference on Windows.
+
+### CI/CD
+- `.github/workflows/dev-short-tests.yml`:
+  - New `cmake-visual-2022-arm64` job on `windows-11-arm`. It runs CMake with `-A ARM64` and warnings as errors, checks the PE machine type of `zstd.exe`, then runs ctest.
+  - New `VS 2022 ARM64 Release` entry in the `msbuild-visual-studio` matrix.
+
+### New Files
+- `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt` and `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.meta.json`: the native ARM64 baseline benchmark results.
+- `ARM64-PORT.md`: this document.
+- No SIMD translation libraries were added.
+
+## Build Steps (ARM64)
+Prerequisites: Visual Studio 2022 or newer with the **MSVC ARM64 build tools** (the ARM64-host toolset on a Windows ARM64 machine) and a **Windows 11 SDK**. CMake and Ninja come from the Visual Studio-bundled "C++ CMake tools" component. There are no third-party dependencies, because zlib, lzma and lz4 are OFF, as in the MSYS2 recipe.
+
+### Build
+```bat
+call "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\18\Community\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvarsarm64.bat"
+cd /d C:\wos-eval\work\zstd
+
+rem 1. CMake + Ninja (mirrors the MSYS2 recipe: build/cmake, Release, shared-linked programs)
+cmake -S build/cmake -B build-arm64 -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DZSTD_PROGRAMS_LINK_SHARED=ON -DZSTD_BUILD_TESTS=ON
+cmake --build build-arm64
+
+rem 2. CMake Visual Studio generator, warnings as errors
+cmake -S build/cmake -B build-arm64-vs -G "Visual Studio 18 2026" -A ARM64 -DCMAKE_COMPILE_WARNING_AS_ERROR=ON -DZSTD_BUILD_TESTS=ON
+cmake --build build-arm64-vs --config Release -- /m
+
+rem 3. MSBuild VS2010 solution (Release and Debug both build clean with /warnaserror)
+msbuild build\VS2010\zstd.sln /t:Rebuild /p:Platform=ARM64 /p:Configuration=Release /p:PlatformToolset=v145 /m /warnaserror
+```
+On a host with Visual Studio 2022, use `-G "Visual Studio 17 2022"` and `/p:PlatformToolset=v143`.
+
+Build output:
+- `build-arm64\{lib,programs,tests}`
+- `build-arm64-vs\{lib,programs,tests}\Release`
+- `build\VS2010\bin\ARM64_{Release,Debug}`
+
+### Run Tests
+```bat
+ctest --test-dir build-arm64 --output-on-failure -j3 --timeout 1500
+
+rem Upstream visual-runtime-tests equivalent (MSBuild output copied into tests\, Git for Windows sh):
+copy build\VS2010\bin\ARM64_Release\*.exe tests\
+cd tests
+set ZSTD_BIN=./zstd.exe
+set DATAGEN_BIN=./datagen.exe
+"C:\Program Files\Git\bin\sh.exe" -e playTests.sh
+fuzzer.exe -T30s
+..\build-arm64-vs\tests\Release\zstreamtest.exe -T30s
+```
+Expected result: all of the checks above pass with 0 failures. The full table is in the Test Results section below.
+
+### Run Benchmarks
+```bat
+set PATH=%CD%\build-arm64\lib;%PATH%
+build-arm64\tests\datagen.exe -g100MB > datagen_100MB.bin
+tar -cf lib_src.tar -C . lib
+build-arm64\programs\zstd.exe -b1e19 -i1 datagen_100MB.bin
+build-arm64\programs\zstd.exe -b1e19 -i1 lib_src.tar
+build-arm64\programs\zstd.exe -b1e19 -i1 -T0 datagen_100MB.bin
+build-arm64\programs\zstd.exe --ultra -b20e22 -i1 lib_src.tar
+build-arm64\tests\fullbench.exe -i1
+```
+The results are recorded in `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt`.
+
